1
00:00:00,039 --> 00:00:02,670
Open Workforce and choose Work entries.

2
00:00:03,119 --> 00:00:07,719
The table separates the worker,
hours, hours type, establishment,

3
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:10,109
context and approval status.

4
00:00:10,470 --> 00:00:15,289
In this training department, the existing
two-hour entry shows No under Approved.

5
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:18,909
We will create a separate example
and follow it from an unapproved

6
00:00:18,909 --> 00:00:21,329
save to a verified approved result.

7
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:25,629
An administrator needs the appropriate
workforce access for these controls.

8
00:00:25,969 --> 00:00:28,219
The earlier example remains unchanged.

9
00:00:28,470 --> 00:00:30,189
Select Add work entry.

10
00:00:30,570 --> 00:00:33,169
In the form, the worker is Matthew Casey.

11
00:00:33,519 --> 00:00:37,530
Set Date to November first,
twenty twenty-six, enter one

12
00:00:37,530 --> 00:00:41,559
point two five Hours, and
choose Standby under Hours type.

13
00:00:42,019 --> 00:00:44,990
Select the training establishment
appropriate to the example.

14
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:48,229
These fields describe this
individual work entry.

15
00:00:48,639 --> 00:00:54,209
Check the worker, date, quantity and hours
type together before continuing, so the

16
00:00:54,209 --> 00:00:56,389
approval will refer to the intended row.

17
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:58,219
Scroll to the bottom of the form.

18
00:00:58,710 --> 00:01:02,869
External source and External id
provide references for this example.

19
00:01:03,299 --> 00:01:06,209
Leave the Approved checkbox
clear for the first save.

20
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:10,150
The Approved payroll cost field
is also blank in this exercise.

21
00:01:10,509 --> 00:01:14,500
Select Save, then find the new
row with the context TRAINING

22
00:01:14,539 --> 00:01:16,299
ONLY, Approval exercise.

23
00:01:16,609 --> 00:01:20,629
Its date, one point two five hours
and Standby type are visible,

24
00:01:20,939 --> 00:01:22,869
and Approved still reads No.

25
00:01:23,180 --> 00:01:26,219
This returned row confirms
the initial saved state.

26
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:30,280
Use the pencil control at the right
of the new exercise row to reopen it.

27
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:33,410
Scroll to Approved and
select the checkbox.

28
00:01:33,809 --> 00:01:37,059
In this view, the table on the
left still shows the earlier

29
00:01:37,059 --> 00:01:41,259
saved value, No, while the form
checkbox on the right is selected.

30
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:43,789
The form change still needs to be saved.

31
00:01:44,209 --> 00:01:48,229
Confirm that this is the intended
training entry, then select Save

32
00:01:48,229 --> 00:01:49,860
to store its approval status.

33
00:01:50,070 --> 00:01:51,820
Reload the Work entries page.

34
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:55,489
The new exercise row now
shows Yes under Approved.

35
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:59,989
The worker, date, one point
two five hours and Standby type

36
00:02:00,029 --> 00:02:01,869
remain visible on that same row.

37
00:02:02,229 --> 00:02:04,869
The earlier two-hour entry still shows No.

38
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:08,780
Compare the complete row when reviewing
an approval, rather than reading a

39
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:11,100
Yes value without its worker and date.

40
00:02:11,450 --> 00:02:15,430
The Approved payroll cost column remains
blank for this software exercise.

41
00:02:15,549 --> 00:02:18,819
Use the two date fields above
the table to focus the review.

42
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:24,480
Set both boundaries to November first,
twenty twenty-six, then select Filter.

43
00:02:24,959 --> 00:02:28,339
The returned table contains the
single exercise entry for that

44
00:02:28,339 --> 00:02:32,940
date, including its Standby hours,
context and Yes approval value.

45
00:02:33,399 --> 00:02:37,460
Changing the date fields alone does
not refresh this table; the Filter

46
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:39,419
button applies the selected range.

47
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:43,540
Check those boundaries when a saved
entry seems to be missing from the list.

48
00:02:43,709 --> 00:02:47,370
This workflow gives a department
a visible saved approval status

49
00:02:47,370 --> 00:02:48,989
for a particular work entry.

50
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:53,780
A security supervisor can review patrol
standby time, a search-and-rescue

51
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:58,100
coordinator can review an exercise
entry, and a community paramedicine

52
00:02:58,129 --> 00:03:01,460
or mental health response team
can review its recorded work.

53
00:03:01,899 --> 00:03:06,210
Wildland contractors, industrial
response teams, and fire and E M S

54
00:03:06,210 --> 00:03:11,130
departments can use the same worker,
date, hours type and context checks.

55
00:03:11,589 --> 00:03:15,509
Agree who reviews entries,
then verify the saved result

56
00:03:15,509 --> 00:03:17,049
in the appropriate date range.
